.SH "Opis szczegółowy"
.PP 

.SH "JSON5 – JSON for Humans"
.PP
[][Build Status] [][Coverage Status]

.PP
JSON5 is an extension to the popular \fRJSON\fP file format that aims to be easier to \fBwrite and maintain \fIby hand\fP (e\&.g\&. for config files)\fP\&. It is \fInot intended\fP to be used for machine-to-machine communication\&. (Keep using JSON or other file formats for that\&. 🙂)

.PP
JSON5 was started in 2012, and as of 2022, now gets \fB\fR>65M downloads/week\fP\fP, ranks in the \fB\fRtop 0\&.1%\fP\fP of the most depended-upon packages on npm, and has been adopted by major projects like \fB\fRChromium\fP, \fRNext\&.js\fP, \fRBabel\fP, \fRRetool\fP, \fRWebStorm\fP, and \fRmore\fP\fP\&. It's also natively supported on \fB\fRApple platforms\fP\fP like \fBMacOS\fP and \fBiOS\fP\&.

.PP
Formally, the \fB\fRJSON5 Data Interchange Format\fP\fP is a superset of JSON (so valid JSON files will always be valid JSON5 files) that expands its syntax to include some productions from [ECMAScript 5\&.1] (ES5)\&. It's also a strict \fIsubset\fP of ES5, so valid JSON5 files will always be valid ES5\&.

.PP
This JavaScript library is a reference implementation for JSON5 parsing and serialization, and is directly used in many of the popular projects mentioned above (where e\&.g\&. extreme performance isn't necessary), but others have created \fRmany other libraries\fP across many other platforms\&.
.SH "Summary of Features"
.PP
The following ECMAScript 5\&.1 features, which are not supported in JSON, have been extended to JSON5\&.
.SS "Objects"
.IP "\(bu" 2
Object keys may be an ECMAScript 5\&.1 \fI[IdentifierName]\fP\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
Objects may have a single trailing comma\&.
.PP
.SS "Arrays"
.IP "\(bu" 2
Arrays may have a single trailing comma\&.
.PP
.SS "Strings"
.IP "\(bu" 2
Strings may be single quoted\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
Strings may span multiple lines by escaping new line characters\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
Strings may include character escapes\&.
.PP
.SS "Numbers"
.IP "\(bu" 2
Numbers may be hexadecimal\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
Numbers may have a leading or trailing decimal point\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
Numbers may be \fRIEEE 754\fP positive infinity, negative infinity, and NaN\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
Numbers may begin with an explicit plus sign\&.
.PP
.SS "Comments"
.IP "\(bu" 2
Single and multi-line comments are allowed\&.
.PP
.SS "White Space"
.IP "\(bu" 2
Additional white space characters are allowed\&.
.PP
.SH "Example"
.PP
Kitchen-sink example:

.PP
.PP
.nf
{
  // comments
  unquoted: 'and you can quote me on that',
  singleQuotes: 'I can use "double quotes" here',
  lineBreaks: "Look, Mom! \\
No \\\\n's!",
  hexadecimal: 0xdecaf,
  leadingDecimalPoint: \&.8675309, andTrailing: 8675309\&.,
  positiveSign: +1,
  trailingComma: 'in objects', andIn: ['arrays',],
  "backwardsCompatible": "with JSON",
}
.fi
.PP

.PP
A more real-world example is \fRthis config file\fP from the Chromium/Blink project\&.
.SH "Specification"
.PP
For a detailed explanation of the JSON5 format, please read the \fRofficial specification\fP\&.
.SH "Installation and Usage"
.PP
.SS "Node\&.js"
.PP
.nf
npm install json5
.fi
.PP
.SS "CommonJS"
.PP
.nf
const JSON5 = require('json5')
.fi
.PP
.SS "Modules"
.PP
.nf
import JSON5 from 'json5'
.fi
.PP
.SS "Browsers"
.SS "UMD"
.PP
.nf
<!\-\- This will create a global `JSON5` variable\&. \-\->
<script src="https://unpkg\&.com/json5@2/dist/index\&.min\&.js"></script>
.fi
.PP
.SS "Modules"
.PP
.nf
<script type="module">
  import JSON5 from 'https://unpkg\&.com/json5@2/dist/index\&.min\&.mjs'
</script>
.fi
.PP
.SH "API"
.PP
The JSON5 API is compatible with the \fRJSON API\fP\&.
.SS "JSON5\&.parse()"
Parses a JSON5 string, constructing the JavaScript value or object described by the string\&. An optional reviver function can be provided to perform a transformation on the resulting object before it is returned\&.
.SS "Syntax"
JSON5\&.parse(text[, reviver])
.SS "Parameters"
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRtext\fP: The string to parse as JSON5\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRreviver\fP: If a function, this prescribes how the value originally produced by parsing is transformed, before being returned\&.
.PP
.SS "Return value"
The object corresponding to the given JSON5 text\&.
.SS "JSON5\&.stringify()"
Converts a JavaScript value to a JSON5 string, optionally replacing values if a replacer function is specified, or optionally including only the specified properties if a replacer array is specified\&.
.SS "Syntax"
JSON5\&.stringify(value[, replacer[, space]]) JSON5\&.stringify(value[, options])
.SS "Parameters"
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRvalue\fP: The value to convert to a JSON5 string\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRreplacer\fP: A function that alters the behavior of the stringification process, or an array of String and Number objects that serve as a whitelist for selecting/filtering the properties of the value object to be included in the JSON5 string\&. If this value is null or not provided, all properties of the object are included in the resulting JSON5 string\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRspace\fP: A String or Number object that's used to insert white space into the output JSON5 string for readability purposes\&. If this is a Number, it indicates the number of space characters to use as white space; this number is capped at 10 (if it is greater, the value is just 10)\&. Values less than 1 indicate that no space should be used\&. If this is a String, the string (or the first 10 characters of the string, if it's longer than that) is used as white space\&. If this parameter is not provided (or is null), no white space is used\&. If white space is used, trailing commas will be used in objects and arrays\&.
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fRoptions\fP: An object with the following properties:
.IP "  \(bu" 4
\fRreplacer\fP: Same as the \fRreplacer\fP parameter\&.
.IP "  \(bu" 4
\fRspace\fP: Same as the \fRspace\fP parameter\&.
.IP "  \(bu" 4
\fRquote\fP: A String representing the quote character to use when serializing strings\&.
.PP

.PP
.SS "Return value"
A JSON5 string representing the value\&.
.SS "Node\&.js \fRrequire()\fP JSON5 files"
When using Node\&.js, you can \fRrequire()\fP JSON5 files by adding the following statement\&.

.PP
.PP
.nf
require('json5/lib/register')
.fi
.PP

.PP
Then you can load a JSON5 file with a Node\&.js \fRrequire()\fP statement\&. For example:

.PP
.PP
.nf
const config = require('\&./config\&.json5')
.fi
.PP
.SH "CLI"
.PP
Since JSON is more widely used than JSON5, this package includes a CLI for converting JSON5 to JSON and for validating the syntax of JSON5 documents\&.
.SS "Installation"
.PP
.nf
npm install \-\-global json5
.fi
.PP
.SS "Usage"
.PP
.nf
json5 [options] <file>
.fi
.PP

.PP
If \fR<file>\fP is not provided, then STDIN is used\&.
.SS "Options:"
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fR-s\fP, \fR--space\fP: The number of spaces to indent or \fRt\fP for tabs
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fR-o\fP, \fR--out-file [file]\fP: Output to the specified file, otherwise STDOUT
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fR-v\fP, \fR--validate\fP: Validate JSON5 but do not output JSON
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fR-V\fP, \fR--version\fP: Output the version number
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fR-h\fP, \fR--help\fP: Output usage information
.PP
.SH "Contributing"
.PP
.SS "Development"
.PP
.nf
git clone https://github\&.com/json5/json5
cd json5
npm install
.fi
.PP

.PP
When contributing code, please write relevant tests and run \fRnpm test\fP and \fRnpm run lint\fP before submitting pull requests\&. Please use an editor that supports \fREditorConfig\fP\&.
.SS "Issues"
To report bugs or request features regarding the JSON5 \fBdata format\fP, please submit an issue to the official \fB\fR\fIspecification\fP repository\fP\fP\&.

.PP
Note that we will never add any features that make JSON5 incompatible with ES5; that compatibility is a fundamental premise of JSON5\&.

.PP
To report bugs or request features regarding this \fBJavaScript implementation\fP of JSON5, please submit an issue to \fB\fIthis\fP repository\fP\&.
.SS "Security Vulnerabilities and Disclosures"
To report a security vulnerability, please follow the follow the guidelines described in our \fBsecurity policy\fP\&.
